rooms_desc ({"You have entered the main hanger and docking bay of the mighty DEATHSTAR.  The sheer size of the room makes you feel insignificant.  Allaround you Stormtroopers bustle to accomplish the various tasks assignedto them by their superiors.  Also visible are the tenacious engineers whostruggle to maintain the high standards and performance capacity of theseemingly infinite numbers of TIE fighters which nearly cover the floorof the hanger bay.  The entire area is kept neat, ordered and impossiblyclean according to the rigorous standards of both the Dark Lord of the Sith, Phil Vader, and even the impossible standards of the Emperor himself,Akira.  This seems to be a place full of tremendous power and you cansense an enormous force which almost overpowers your senses.  ","     You have entered Lord Vader's conference chamber.  This is ahuge spotless room with a single, long, carbon black table in thecenter.  Twenty comfortable looking chairs surround the table, one for each of the Galactic Empire's Admirals.  At the end of the tablesit two imposing, high-backed seats which resemble thrones.  One ofthese seats is reserved for the Dark Lord Phil Vader, and the other for the Emperor, Akira.  You are overwhelmed by the beautiful, yet simple decor of the chamber and await the arrival of your masters.  Youpray that they find you acceptable...it would be tragic if they did not.  Two Stormtroopers align each of the exits, and you find yourself enthralled by the mere sight of the two crimson-clad RoyalGuards who stand as sentries at the northern exit...the entrance tothe enigmatic Lord Vader's personal chamber.  You can feel the enormous rush of energy of the Dark Side of the Force which flowsfrom that direction.","     This is the room where the great Phil Vader goes to meditate aftercommanding the Imperial troops throughout the galaxy.  This is anothersimple, yet beautifully decorated room inside of the mighty DEATH STAR.The room is almost entirely empty except for the HUGE chamber whichoccupies the center of the room.  Inside of this chamber is where LordVader goes to escape the pressures of being second in charge of the galaxy.  Only Phil Vader himself has access to this area of the DEATH STAH.  Here, as before, you are mezmorized by the impressivenessof the crimson Royal Guards who stand watch at every entrance.  Youcannot begin to fathom the sheer dark power of the Force which rushesfrom the east exit.  The fear you feel is much to great to allow you to pass through this entry.","You are crushed like a cockroach by the power of the Dark Side.		You were warned.",0,0,0,0,0,0,})
